Eager: a list comprehension runs to its end before the next one starts
    map(1) map(2) map(3) map(4) select(10) select(20) select(30) select(40)
 1. [times_ten(x) for ...], then [x for ... if big(x)]       [20, 30, 40]
Lazy: generator expressions interleave, and islice stops at the second hit
    map(1) select(10) map(2) select(20) map(3) select(30)
 2. list(islice((x for x in (...) if big(x)), 2))            [20, 30]

An endless source: itertools.count, which only a lazy chain can map over
 3. islice((x for x in (x * 2 for x in count(1)) if % 3), 3) [6, 12, 18]
 4. filter(..., map(double, count(1))); map calls it took    [[6, 12, 18], 9]
 5. list(takewhile(lambda x: x < 4, count(1)))               [1, 2, 3]
 6. list(islice(batched(count(1), 2), 2))                    [(1, 2), (3, 4)]
 7. islice((x * 2 for x in count(1) if x % 2 == 0), 3)       [4, 8, 12]
 8. islice((x * i for i, x in enumerate(count(1))), 3)       [0, 2, 6]
 9. list(islice(zip(count(1), "abc"), 2))                    [(1, 'a'), (2, 'b')]
10. islice(unique(x % 3 for x in count(1)), 3)               [1, 2, 0]
11. islice(chain.from_iterable([x, -x] for x in count), 4)   [1, -1, 2, -2]
12. islice(dropwhile(lambda x: x < 5, count(1)), 2)          [5, 6]

Which objects are lazy, and which calls run the chain
13. type(genexp), type(map(...)), type(filter(...))          ['generator', 'map', 'filter']
14. type(islice(count(1), 2)), type(list(islice(...)))       ['islice', 'list']
15. list(islice((x * x for x in count(1)), 3))  (list = force) [1, 4, 9]
16. type([x for x in range(4)]), type(list(map(...)))        ['list', 'list']
17. 5 in count(1), sum(x * 2 for x in range(1, 4))           [True, 12]
18. len(count(1)) raises; length_hint(iter([1,2,3])), (map)  ['TypeError', 3, 0]
19. e = (x * 2 for x in count(1)); next(e), next(e)          [2, 4]
20. type(e).__mro__ names, isinstance(e, Iterator)           [['generator', 'object'], True]
